  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Nortoxiferine, dihydro- and CHP-134, mediated through the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including Nortoxiferine, dihydro-, which appears to interact with the proteasome complex. The pathway involves a series of molecular interactions, where Nortoxiferine, dihydro- acts as a target of multiple compounds, ultimately leading to the activation or modulation of CHP-134. The scores from the paths indicate a consistent level of confidence in this relationship, suggesting that Nortoxiferine, dihydro- may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving the proteasome regulatory subunit 14. The evidence supports a plausible pathway where Nortoxiferine, dihydro- influences the proteasome complex, which in turn affects CHP-134. The integration of these findings highlights the importance of the proteasome regulatory subunit 14 in mediating the interaction between Nortoxiferine, dihydro- and CHP-134.",
